-- The unique table of all definitions.
`all definitions` MEANS append `s3 definitions` (append `s38 definitions` `definitions in the other sections`)

-- The sections whose definitions apply in all Acts and subordinate instruments (s 38 and the sections that continue it).
`sections whose definitions apply in all Acts and subordinate instruments` MEANS
    LIST "s 38", "s 38A", "s 38AB", "s 38B", "s 38BA", "s 38D", "s 38E", "s 38EA(1)", "s 38F", "s 38FA", "s 38G", "s 38H", "s 38I", "s 38J", "s 38K", "s 38L"

GIVEN section IS A STRING, term IS A STRING, table IS A LIST OF VicDefinition
GIVETH A MAYBE VicDefinition
`find the definition of a term in a section` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN d YIELD d's `defined in` EQUALS section AND elem term (d's `terms`)) table
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST d

GIVEN term IS A STRING, table IS A LIST OF VicDefinition
GIVETH A MAYBE VicDefinition
`find the definition of a term in the sections that apply in all Acts` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN d YIELD elem (d's `defined in`) `sections whose definitions apply in all Acts and subordinate instruments` AND elem term (d's `terms`)) table
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST d

-- s 3 and s 38 begin "unless inconsistent with the context or subject-matter" and "unless the contrary intention appears".
-- The definition a term has is given; when the unless-clause applies, the text does not say what the term means.
-- src:31 | 3 Definitions
-- src:32 | In this Act, unless inconsistent with the context or subject-matter—
@ref s 3 opening words (src:31-32)
-- src:558 | 38 Definitions
-- src:559 | In all Acts and subordinate instruments, unless the contrary intention appears—
@ref s 38 opening words (src:558-559)
GIVEN section IS A STRING, term IS A STRING, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicDefinition
`meaning of a term defined in a section` MEANS
    IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `find the definition of a term in a section` section term `all definitions`

-- src:558 | 38 Definitions
-- src:559 | In all Acts and subordinate instruments, unless the contrary intention appears—
@ref s 38 opening words (src:558-559)
GIVEN term IS A STRING, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicDefinition
`meaning of a term in all Acts and subordinate instruments` MEANS
    IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `find the definition of a term in the sections that apply in all Acts` term `all definitions`

-- src:558 | 38 Definitions
-- src:559 | In all Acts and subordinate instruments, unless the contrary intention appears—
@ref s 38 opening words (src:558-559)
GIVEN section IS A STRING, term IS A STRING, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicDefinitionKind
`kind of the definition of a term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `meaning of a term defined in a section` section term contraryIntentionAppears
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d's `kind`)

-- src:558 | 38 Definitions
-- src:559 | In all Acts and subordinate instruments, unless the contrary intention appears—
@ref s 38 opening words (src:558-559)
GIVEN section IS A STRING, term IS A STRING, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`wording of the definition of a term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `meaning of a term defined in a section` section term contraryIntentionAppears
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d's `the wording after the verb`)

-- src:558 | 38 Definitions
-- src:559 | In all Acts and subordinate instruments, unless the contrary intention appears—
@ref s 38 opening words (src:558-559)
GIVEN section IS A STRING, term IS A STRING, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`members the definition of a term names` MEANS
    CONSIDER `meaning of a term defined in a section` section term contraryIntentionAppears
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d's `the members it names`)

-- Whether something is within a term: a "means" definition that names members closes the list (anything else is not within it);
-- an "includes" definition that names members leaves the list open (a member is within it, anything else is not covered);
-- a definition that points elsewhere, or names no members, is not covered.
-- src:558 | 38 Definitions
-- src:559 | In all Acts and subordinate instruments, unless the contrary intention appears—
@ref s 38 opening words (src:558-559)
GIVEN section IS A STRING, term IS A STRING, thing IS A STRING, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`thing is within the term as defined` MEANS
    CONSIDER `meaning of a term defined in a section` section term contraryIntentionAppears
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        BRANCH
            IF elem thing (d's `the members it names`) THEN JUST TRUE
            IF d's `kind` EQUALS VicMeans AND NOT (null (d's `the members it names`)) THEN JUST FALSE
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
